    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-16j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16J Delegation by Commission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982#sec-16j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate all or any of its\nfunctions or powers under this Act to a Commissioner.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n(2) In exercising a delegated function or power, the delegate must\ncomply with any written directions of the Commission.\n(3) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the\nconstitution of the Commission.\n(4) The delegation may be varied or revoked by resolution of the\nCommission (whether or not there has been a change in the\nconstitution of the Commission).\n(5) A certificate signed by the Chair stating any matter with respect to\nthe delegation is prima facie evidence of the matter.\n(6) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in\nsubsection (5) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nduly given unless the contrary is established.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate all or any of its\nfunctions or powers under this Act to a Commissioner.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n(2) In exercising a delegated function or power, the delegate must\ncomply with any written directions of the Commission.\n(3) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the\nconstitution of the Commission.\n(4) The delegation may be varied or revoked by resolution of the\nCommission (whether or not there has been a change in the\nconstitution of the Commission).\n(5) A certificate signed by the Chair stating any matter with respect to\nthe delegation is prima facie evidence of the matter.\n(6) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in\nsubsection (5) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nduly given unless the contrary is established.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-16j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-16j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-16j-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-16j-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-16j-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-16j-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1cc2519d4609f7afda4deb9b0af6dd2f932c361ff50f7812aafec9a4c51d9a68"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982#sec-16j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16J Delegation by Commission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate all or any of its\nfunctions or powers under this Act to a Commissioner.\nNote:\nSections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain\nprovisions relating to delegations.\n(2) In exercising a delegated function or power, the delegate must\ncomply with any written directions of the Commission.\n(3) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the\nconstitution of the Commission.\n(4) The delegation may be varied or revoked by resolution of the\nCommission (whether or not there has been a change in the\nconstitution of the Commission).\n(5) A certificate signed by the Chair stating any matter with respect to\nthe delegation is prima facie evidence of the matter.\n(6) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in\nsubsection (5) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nduly given unless the contrary is established."
    },
