      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If an appointed member of the Council:\n(a) becomes bankrupt, applies to take the benefit of any law for\nthe relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors, compounds with\nhis or her creditors or makes an assignment of his or her\nremuneration for their benefit; or\n(b) is absent, except on leave granted by the Council, from 3\nconsecutive meetings of the Council otherwise than on\nbusiness of the Council undertaken with the approval of the\nCouncil;\nthe Minister shall terminate the appointment of that member.",
