      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may terminate the appointment of the CEO:\n(a) for misbehaviour; or\n(b) if the CEO is unable to perform the duties of the CEO’s\noffice because of physical or mental incapacity; or\n(c) if the CEO’s conduct or behaviour amounts to serious\nmisconduct by the CEO."
    },
    {
