    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29C(1A) Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982#sec-29c-ss-1a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) Without limiting the circumstances in which the CEO’s conduct or\nbehaviour amounts to serious misconduct by the CEO, the CEO’s\nconduct or behaviour amounts to serious misconduct by the CEO\nin the following circumstances:\n(a) both:\n(i) the conduct or behaviour constitutes a breach of the\nAPS Code of Conduct; and\n(ii) the Minister is satisfied that the breach is serious\nenough to justify termination of the CEO’s\nappointment;\n(b) the conduct or behaviour constitutes unlawful discrimination\n(within the meaning of the Australian Human Rights\nCommission Act 1986);\n(c) an investigation report (within the meaning of the National\nAnti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) includes a finding or\nopinion that the CEO has engaged, is engaging or will\nengage in:\n(i) corrupt conduct (within the meaning of that Act); or\n(ii) conduct that could constitute or involve corrupt conduct.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) Without limiting the circumstances in which the CEO’s conduct or\nbehaviour amounts to serious misconduct by the CEO, the CEO’s\nconduct or behaviour amounts to serious misconduct by the CEO\nin the following circumstances:\n(a) both:\n(i) the conduct or behaviour constitutes a breach of the\nAPS Code of Conduct; and\n(ii) the Minister is satisfied that the breach is serious\nenough to justify termination of the CEO’s\nappointment;\n(b) the conduct or behaviour constitutes unlawful discrimination\n(within the meaning of the Australian Human Rights\nCommission Act 1986);\n(c) an investigation report (within the meaning of the National\nAnti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) includes a finding or\nopinion that the CEO has engaged, is engaging or will\nengage in:\n(i) corrupt conduct (within the meaning of that Act); or\n(ii) conduct that could constitute or involve corrupt conduct.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-descriptionlogic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-deontic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "155809c22184d033868f8625d71b9aa837a6c26513a4bed75adfff7065fe3ace",
      "skos:note": "Termination of appointment under certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982#sec-29c-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29C(1A) Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) Without limiting the circumstances in which the CEO’s conduct or\nbehaviour amounts to serious misconduct by the CEO, the CEO’s\nconduct or behaviour amounts to serious misconduct by the CEO\nin the following circumstances:\n(a) both:\n(i) the conduct or behaviour constitutes a breach of the\nAPS Code of Conduct; and\n(ii) the Minister is satisfied that the breach is serious\nenough to justify termination of the CEO’s\nappointment;\n(b) the conduct or behaviour constitutes unlawful discrimination\n(within the meaning of the Australian Human Rights\nCommission Act 1986);\n(c) an investigation report (within the meaning of the National\nAnti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) includes a finding or\nopinion that the CEO has engaged, is engaging or will\nengage in:\n(i) corrupt conduct (within the meaning of that Act); or\n(ii) conduct that could constitute or involve corrupt conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to terminate appointment",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1A) Without limiting the circumstances in which the CEO’s conduct or behaviour amounts to serious misconduct by the CEO...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Minister must terminate the CEO's appointment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "ClassInclusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Class inclusion for 'serious misconduct'",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) both: (i) the conduct or behaviour constitutes a breach of the APS Code of Conduct; and (ii) the Minister is satisfied that the breach is serious enough to justify termination of the CEO’s appointment;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The CEO's conduct or behaviour amounts to serious misconduct if it breaches the APS Code of Conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal overlap between investigation report and CEO's conduct",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) an investigation report (within the meaning of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) includes a finding or opinion that the CEO has engaged, is engaging or will engage in:...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The CEO's conduct overlaps with the investigation report's findings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to terminate appointment under certain conditions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the conduct or behaviour constitutes unlawful discrimination (within the meaning of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Minister may terminate the CEO's appointment if it is unlawful discrimination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-descriptionlogic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "ClassInclusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Class inclusion for 'unlawful discrimination'",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the conduct or behaviour constitutes unlawful discrimination (within the meaning of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The CEO's conduct is a type of unlawful discrimination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-1a-logic-deontic-6",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to investigate and report on corrupt conduct",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) an investigation report (within the meaning of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) includes a finding or opinion that the CEO has engaged, is engaging or will engage in:...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Minister must investigate and report on the CEO's corrupt conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29C(2) Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982#sec-29c-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of the CEO\nif:\n(a) the CEO:\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n(iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of the CEO\nif:\n(a) the CEO:\n(i) becomes bankrupt; or\n(ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors; or\n(iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-29c-ss-2-norm"
        },
