    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Arrangements relating to staff",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982#sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CEO may arrange with an Agency Head (within the meaning\nof the Public Service Act 1999) or with a body (other than a\ncompany or an association) established for a public purpose by or\nunder a law of the Commonwealth for the services of officers or\nemployees of the Agency or body to be made available to the CEO\nin relation to the CEO’s functions.\n(2) The CEO may enter into an arrangement with the appropriate\nauthority of a State or Territory for the services of officers or\nemployees of the Public Service of the State or Territory, or of a\nbody established for a public purpose by or under a law of the State\nor Territory, to be made available to the CEO in relation to the\nCEO’s functions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The CEO may arrange with an Agency Head (within the meaning\nof the Public Service Act 1999) or with a body (other than a\ncompany or an association) established for a public purpose by or\nunder a law of the Commonwealth for the services of officers or\nemployees of the Agency or body to be made available to the CEO\nin relation to the CEO’s functions.\n(2) The CEO may enter into an arrangement with the appropriate\nauthority of a State or Territory for the services of officers or\nemployees of the Public Service of the State or Territory, or of a\nbody established for a public purpose by or under a law of the State\nor Territory, to be made available to the CEO in relation to the\nCEO’s functions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-31-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-31-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "978b1334c0ba4ce0f763e32e3d31e9c0804411cd2119ddb869729d1f9112d8b8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982#sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Arrangements relating to staff",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The CEO may arrange with an Agency Head (within the meaning\nof the Public Service Act 1999) or with a body (other than a\ncompany or an association) established for a public purpose by or\nunder a law of the Commonwealth for the services of officers or\nemployees of the Agency or body to be made available to the CEO\nin relation to the CEO’s functions.\n(2) The CEO may enter into an arrangement with the appropriate\nauthority of a State or Territory for the services of officers or\nemployees of the Public Service of the State or Territory, or of a\nbody established for a public purpose by or under a law of the State\nor Territory, to be made available to the CEO in relation to the\nCEO’s functions."
    },
